---
import Base from '../layouts/Base.astro';
---
<Base title="The Emergency Preparedness Guide" description="A practical e-book and printable household checklists, fridge card, and wallet cards from Critical Latitude. Explore the guide and buy on Payhip.">
<div class="guide-page">
<svg class="icon-definitions" xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg" aria-hidden="true">
    <defs>
      <symbol id="icon-book" viewBox="0 0 32 32"><path d="M16 8c-4-3-9-3-13-2v21c5-1 9-1 13 2 4-3 8-3 13-2V6c-4-1-9-1-13 2Zm0 0v21M6 3c4-.5 7 .5 10 2 3-1.5 6-2.5 10-2"/></symbol>
      <symbol id="icon-fridge" viewBox="0 0 32 32"><rect x="7" y="2" width="18" height="27" rx="2"/><path d="M7 11h18M11 6v2m0 7v6M10 29v2m12-2v2"/></symbol>
      <symbol id="icon-wallet" viewBox="0 0 32 32"><path d="m5 11 16-8 4 8M7 9l15-3M3 12h25v17H3z"/><path d="M28 17h-8v7h8"/><circle cx="23" cy="20.5" r=".8"/></symbol>
      <symbol id="icon-arrow" viewBox="0 0 24 24"><path d="M4 12h16m-6-6 6 6-6 6"/></symbol>
      <symbol id="icon-check" viewBox="0 0 24 24"><path d="m5 12 4 4L19 6"/></symbol>
      <symbol id="icon-download" viewBox="0 0 24 24"><path d="M12 3v12m-5-5 5 5 5-5M4 16v5h16v-5"/></symbol>
      <symbol id="icon-family" viewBox="0 0 32 32"><circle cx="9" cy="8" r="4"/><circle cx="24" cy="8" r="4"/><circle cx="16" cy="18" r="3"/><path d="M2 27v-8a7 7 0 0 1 11-6m6 0a7 7 0 0 1 11 6v8M10 30v-4a6 6 0 0 1 12 0v4"/></symbol>
      <symbol id="icon-care" viewBox="0 0 32 32"><path d="M16 27 4 15C-3 6 8-2 16 7 24-2 35 6 28 15Z"/><path d="M16 10v10m-5-5h10"/></symbol>
      <symbol id="icon-home" viewBox="0 0 32 32"><path d="m2 15 14-12 14 12M6 12v17h20V12M12 29V19h8v10"/></symbol>
    </defs>
  </svg>
    
    <section class="hero topographic" id="home" aria-labelledby="hero-title">
      <div class="container">
        <div class="hero-grid">
          <div class="hero-copy">
            <p class="eyebrow"><span class="status-square" aria-hidden="true"></span> LARGE-PRINT EDITION</p>
            <h1 id="hero-title">THE EMERGENCY<br><em>PREPAREDNESS</em><br>GUIDE</h1>
            <p class="hero-description">Disaster-by-disaster checklists, medication and medical-equipment plans, and fill-in worksheets — built on FEMA, Red Cross, and Ready.gov guidance.</p>
            <div class="hero-actions">
              <a class="button" href="https://payhip.com/b/GWENV">Get the Guide on Payhip<svg class="icon" aria-hidden="true"><use href="#icon-arrow"/></svg></a>
              <a class="button button-outline" href="#inside">See what's inside</a>
            </div>
            <p class="hero-note"><svg class="icon" aria-hidden="true"><use href="#icon-download"/></svg> Digital download. Yours to read, print, and keep.</p>
          </div>
          <div class="product-scene" role="img" aria-label="The Critical Latitude large-print guide on a tablet, a cream go-bag checklist, a red fridge card, and two emergency wallet cards.">
            <div class="scene-orbit" aria-hidden="true"></div>
            <div class="scene-coordinates" aria-hidden="true">A PLAN WORTH HAVING. BEFORE YOU NEED IT.</div>
            <div class="tablet" aria-hidden="true">
              <span class="tablet-camera"></span>
              <div class="ebook-cover topographic">
                <span class="cover-tag">LARGE-PRINT EDITION</span>
                <div class="cover-title">THE<br>EMERGENCY<br><span>PREPAREDNESS</span><br>GUIDE</div>
                <p>Disaster-by-disaster checklists, medication and medical-equipment plans, and fill-in worksheets.</p>
                <div class="cover-footer"><img src="/logo.png" width="39" height="39" alt=""><div>CRITICAL LATITUDE<small>PREPAREDNESS SERIES</small></div></div>
              </div>
            </div>
            <div class="mini-page paper" aria-hidden="true">
              <span class="paper-kicker">GO-BAG CHECKLIST</span><h2>YOUR GO-BAG</h2>
              <p>One bag, packed now, by the door you'd actually leave from.</p>
              <h3>DOCUMENTS &amp; MONEY</h3>
              <ul class="checklist"><li>Photocopies of ID, Medicare/insurance cards, and prescription list</li><li>Copies of deed/lease, insurance policies, and key contacts</li><li>Cash in small bills</li><li>Spare house and car keys</li></ul>
              <h3>HEALTH — PACK THIS SECTION FIRST</h3>
              <ul class="checklist"><li>Medication plan and labeled supplies</li><li>Written medication list</li><li>Spare eyeglasses</li><li>First aid kit, hand sanitizer, appropriate masks</li></ul>
              <div class="paper-footer"><span>CRITICAL LATITUDE</span><span>SAMPLE PAGE</span></div>
            </div>
            <div class="mini-fridge paper" aria-hidden="true">
              <div class="mini-fridge-title">WHEN DISASTER STRIKES <small>FRIDGE CARD</small></div>
              <div class="mini-fridge-grid"><div><b>EARTHQUAKE</b><p>DROP · COVER · HOLD ON</p><b>TORNADO WARNING</b><p>Interior room, lowest floor</p></div><div><b>BEFORE YOU WALK ANYWHERE</b><p>Shoes on. Flashlight ready.</p><b>MY OUT-OF-AREA CONTACT</b><span class="writing-line"></span></div></div>
              <div class="mini-red-footer">KEEP EMERGENCY CONTACTS WITH YOU</div>
            </div>
            <div class="mini-wallet wallet-one paper" aria-hidden="true"><b>EMERGENCY MEDICAL INFO</b><span>NAME</span><span>MEDICATIONS</span><i>KEEP WITH YOU</i></div>
            <div class="mini-wallet wallet-two paper" aria-hidden="true"><b>EMERGENCY CONTACTS</b><span>CONTACT 1</span><span>PHONE</span><i>CRITICAL LATITUDE</i></div>
          </div>
        </div>
        <div class="hero-bottom">
          <p class="bundle-title">E-BOOK <span>+</span> PRINTABLES</p>
          <ul class="bundle-items" aria-label="Included in the bundle">
            <li><svg class="icon" aria-hidden="true"><use href="#icon-book"/></svg><span>Large-Print Guide</span></li>
            <li><svg class="icon" aria-hidden="true"><use href="#icon-fridge"/></svg><span>Fridge Card</span></li>
            <li><svg class="icon" aria-hidden="true"><use href="#icon-wallet"/></svg><span>Wallet Cards</span></li>
          </ul>
        </div>
      </div>
    </section>

    
    <section class="credibility" aria-label="Sources and format">
      <div class="container credibility-inner"><p>Built on official guidance from <strong>FEMA <span>·</span> American Red Cross <span>·</span> Ready.gov</strong></p><p class="format-line">Instant download <span>·</span> Print at home <span>·</span> US Letter</p></div>
    </section>

    
    <section class="section inside-section" id="inside" aria-labelledby="inside-title">
      <div class="container">
        <div class="section-heading"><div><p class="eyebrow">01 / THE COMPLETE KIT</p><h2 id="inside-title">WHAT'S <em>INSIDE</em></h2></div><p>Read it once. Fill it in together.<br>Keep the important parts within reach.</p></div>
        <div class="inside-grid">
          <article class="kit-card"><div class="kit-card-top"><svg class="icon" aria-hidden="true"><use href="#icon-book"/></svg><span>01 / READ &amp; PLAN</span></div><h3>LARGE-PRINT E-BOOK</h3><p>The details you need, in type you can actually read.</p><ul class="feature-list"><li>Practical household planning chapters</li><li>Disaster-by-disaster checklists</li><li>Medication and equipment worksheets</li></ul><div class="kit-card-foot">YOUR HOUSEHOLD REFERENCE <span aria-hidden="true">↗</span></div></article>
          <article class="kit-card"><div class="kit-card-top"><svg class="icon" aria-hidden="true"><use href="#icon-fridge"/></svg><span>02 / PRINT &amp; POST</span></div><h3>THE FRIDGE CARD</h3><p>“When Disaster Strikes.” Quick actions where everyone can find them.</p><ul class="feature-list"><li>Earthquake, tornado, and flood actions</li><li>A short before-you-leave checklist</li><li>Your out-of-area contact</li></ul><div class="kit-card-foot">ON THE FRIDGE. IN PLAIN SIGHT. <span aria-hidden="true">↗</span></div></article>
          <article class="kit-card"><div class="kit-card-top"><svg class="icon" aria-hidden="true"><use href="#icon-wallet"/></svg><span>03 / FILL IN &amp; CARRY</span></div><h3>THE WALLET CARDS</h3><p>A little paper backup for the information usually in your phone.</p><ul class="feature-list"><li>Emergency Medical Info card</li><li>Emergency Contacts card</li><li>Space for the details that matter</li></ul><div class="kit-card-foot">ESSENTIALS THAT GO WITH YOU <span aria-hidden="true">↗</span></div></article>
        </div>
      </div>
    </section>

    
    <section class="section preview-section" id="preview" aria-labelledby="preview-title">
      <div class="container">
        <div class="section-heading"><div><p class="eyebrow">02 / TAKE A CLOSER LOOK</p><h2 id="preview-title">PREVIEW A PAGE.</h2></div><p>Clear checklists. Space for your details.<br>Made for the kitchen table, not just a screen.</p></div>
        <div class="preview-grid">
          <article class="sample-page paper" aria-labelledby="sample-title">
            <header><p class="paper-kicker">GO-BAG CHECKLIST</p><h3 id="sample-title">YOUR GO-BAG</h3><p>One bag, packed now, by the door you'd actually leave from. Use a wheeled bag or backpack you can genuinely carry. If it's too heavy to lift, it's packed wrong.</p></header>
            <h4 class="paper-bar">DOCUMENTS &amp; MONEY</h4>
            <ul class="checklist">
              <li>Photocopies of ID, Medicare/insurance cards, and prescription list (in a zip-top bag)</li>
              <li>Copies of deed/lease, insurance policies, and key contacts (or a USB drive with scans)</li>
              <li>Cash in small bills — ATMs and card readers fail with the power</li>
              <li>Spare house and car keys</li>
            </ul>
            <h4 class="paper-bar">HEALTH — PACK THIS SECTION FIRST</h4>
            <ul class="checklist">
              <li>Medication supplies planned with your pharmacist, with original labels where possible</li>
              <li>Written medication list: drug, dose, schedule, prescriber</li>
              <li>Spare eyeglasses (an old prescription beats none)</li>
              <li>Hearing aid batteries or charger</li>
              <li>Spare cane / walking aid if you use one</li>
              <li>Denture care, incontinence supplies, any daily medical items</li>
              <li>First aid kit, hand sanitizer, appropriate masks</li>
            </ul>
            <footer class="paper-footer"><span>CRITICAL LATITUDE</span><span>GO-BAG CHECKLIST · GO-BAG</span><span>SAMPLE PAGE</span></footer>
          </article>
          <div class="preview-extras">
            <article class="fridge-card paper" aria-labelledby="fridge-title">
              <header class="alert-header"><h3 id="fridge-title">WHEN DISASTER STRIKES</h3><span>FRIDGE CARD</span></header>
              <div class="fridge-columns">
                <div><h4>EARTHQUAKE — SHAKING STARTS</h4><ol><li><strong>DROP</strong> — or sit and lean forward</li><li><strong>COVER</strong> head &amp; neck</li><li><strong>HOLD ON</strong> until it stops</li></ol><h4>TORNADO WARNING</h4><ol><li>Interior room, lowest floor</li><li>Away from windows</li><li>Cover your head</li></ol><h4>FLOOD / WATER ON ROAD</h4><ol><li>Don't drive into water</li><li>Move to high ground</li></ol></div>
                <div><h4 class="ink-heading">BEFORE YOU WALK ANYWHERE</h4><ul><li>Sturdy shoes ON (glass, debris)</li><li>Flashlight — never candles</li><li>Smell gas? Get out, don't flip switches</li></ul><h4 class="ink-heading">THEN</h4><ul><li>TEXT (don't call): “I'm OK, I'm at ___”</li><li>Radio ON for instructions</li><li>Grab go-bag if leaving</li><li>Generator placement: follow current official safety guidance</li></ul><h4 class="ink-heading contact-heading">MY OUT-OF-AREA CONTACT</h4><span class="writing-line" aria-label="Blank space for your contact"></span></div>
              </div>
              <footer class="fridge-footer">WRITE IN YOUR LOCAL EMERGENCY AND SUPPORT CONTACTS</footer>
            </article>
            <div class="wallet-preview-grid">
              <article class="wallet-card paper"><header><h3>EMERGENCY MEDICAL INFO</h3><span>IN CASE I NEED HELP</span></header><div class="wallet-fields"><span>NAME</span><span>DATE OF BIRTH</span><span>BLOOD TYPE</span><span>CONDITIONS</span><span>ALLERGIES</span><span>MEDICATIONS</span></div><footer>SEE MEDICATION LIST IN WALLET / GO-BAG</footer></article>
              <article class="wallet-card paper"><header><h3>EMERGENCY CONTACTS</h3><span>PLEASE CALL</span></header><div class="wallet-fields"><span>CONTACT 1</span><span>PHONE</span><span>CONTACT 2</span><span>PHONE</span><span>DOCTOR</span><span>PHARMACY</span></div><footer>CRITICAL LATITUDE · PREPAREDNESS SERIES</footer></article>
            </div>
            <div class="preview-caption"><span class="caption-line" aria-hidden="true"></span><p>A plan on paper.<br><strong>Even when the power is out.</strong></p></div>
          </div>
        </div>
        <p class="preview-note">Sample layouts shown. Printables are designed for US Letter paper. Follow current instructions from your local emergency authorities.</p>
      </div>
    </section>

    
    <section class="section audience-section" aria-labelledby="audience-title">
      <div class="container"><p class="eyebrow">03 / WHO IT'S FOR</p><h2 id="audience-title">YOUR HOUSEHOLD.<br><em>YOUR PLAN.</em></h2>
        <div class="audience-grid">
          <article><svg class="icon" aria-hidden="true"><use href="#icon-care"/></svg><h3>Seniors and caregivers</h3><p>Keep medications, medical equipment, and the people you rely on in the same plan. Large print makes it easier to work through together.</p></article>
          <article><svg class="icon" aria-hidden="true"><use href="#icon-family"/></svg><h3>Families with kids</h3><p>Write down who to call, what to pack, and where to meet. Give everyone a plan they can find and understand.</p></article>
          <article><svg class="icon" aria-hidden="true"><use href="#icon-home"/></svg><h3>Anyone in hurricane, tornado, or wildfire country</h3><p>Start with the risks where you live. Work through practical checklists for storms, earthquakes, floods, and power outages.</p></article>
        </div>
      </div>
    </section>

    
    <section class="section pricing-section" id="pricing" aria-labelledby="pricing-title">
      <div class="container"><div class="pricing-card"><div class="pricing-intro"><p class="eyebrow">ONE HOUSEHOLD. ONE PRACTICAL KIT.</p><h2 id="pricing-title">START WITH<br><em>A PLAN.</em></h2><p>Start with a checklist. End with a plan your household can use.</p><div class="pricing-brand"><img src="/logo.png" width="66" height="66" alt="Critical Latitude"><span>PREPAREDNESS<br>SERIES / DIGITAL EDITION</span></div></div>
        <div class="pricing-offer"><h3>E-BOOK + PRINTABLES</h3><p class="purchase-type">One purchase. The complete digital kit.</p><ul class="feature-list"><li>Large-print e-book</li><li>Disaster checklists &amp; fill-in worksheets</li><li>“When Disaster Strikes” fridge card</li><li>Medical info &amp; contact wallet cards</li><li>US Letter files to print at home</li></ul>
          
          <a class="button button-checkout" href="https://payhip.com/b/GWENV">Get the Complete Guide <svg class="icon" aria-hidden="true"><use href="#icon-arrow"/></svg></a>
          <p class="purchase-note">See the current price, included files, and download terms on Payhip.</p>
          
        </div></div></div>
    </section>

    
    <section class="section faq-section" id="faq" aria-labelledby="faq-title">
      <div class="container faq-layout"><div><p class="eyebrow">05 / FREQUENTLY ASKED QUESTIONS</p><h2 id="faq-title">BEFORE<br>YOU <em>BEGIN.</em></h2><p class="faq-intro">A digital guide.<br>Something useful to keep on paper.</p></div>
        <div class="faq-list">
          <details class="faq-item" open><summary><span>What file format will I receive?</span><span class="faq-symbol" aria-hidden="true"></span></summary><div class="faq-answer"><p>The e-book and printables are PDF files. Read the guide on your computer or tablet, then print the checklists, fridge card, and wallet cards you want to keep close.</p></div></details>
          <details class="faq-item"><summary><span>Can I print it on my home printer?</span><span class="faq-symbol" aria-hidden="true"></span></summary><div class="faq-answer"><p>Yes. The printables are designed for standard US Letter paper. Choose “Actual size” in your print settings. Print as many copies as your household needs.</p></div></details>
          <details class="faq-item"><summary><span>Are future updates included?</span><span class="faq-symbol" aria-hidden="true"></span></summary><div class="faq-answer"><p>The purchase is for the edition listed at checkout. An update schedule has not been announced. Check the product listing for any included updates before purchasing.</p></div></details>
          <details class="faq-item"><summary><span>Who is this guide for?</span><span class="faq-symbol" aria-hidden="true"></span></summary><div class="faq-answer"><p>It is written for US households, including older adults, caregivers, and families with children. Large print, medication worksheets, and clear checklists make it a practical place to start. No previous preparedness experience is needed.</p></div></details>
          <details class="faq-item"><summary><span>What is the refund policy?</span><span class="faq-symbol" aria-hidden="true"></span></summary><div class="faq-answer"><p>Review the refund policy displayed at checkout before you pay. The current product listing and checkout provide the purchase terms.</p></div></details>
        </div>
      </div>
    </section>
  
</div>
</Base>
